.TH MAPS-LOGGER.ENV 5 "20 July 2026" "maps-apps 1.0.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
maps-logger.env \- environment configuration for the Maps MQTT value logger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/maps-logger/env
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B maps-logger.service
systemd unit reads
.I /etc/maps-logger/env
as an EnvironmentFile.  The file configures the MQTT broker subscription, output format,
output directory, disk-space warning threshold, and broker authentication and TLS.
.PP
Use one
.B NAME=value
assignment per line.  Empty lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored by systemd.
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_URL
MQTT broker URL.  This value is required.  The packaged configuration uses
.BR tcp://127.0.0.1:1883 .
Use
.B ssl://
for TLS or mutual TLS.  The logger requests the Message-JSON transformation through its
client id, so no host-wide server transformation rule is required.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_TOPIC
MQTT topic filter, or several filters separated by commas.  The packaged default is
.BR # .
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_QOS
Subscription QoS.  Valid values are 0, 1, and 2.  The default is 1.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_FORMAT
Output format.  Valid values are
.B csv
and
.BR json .
JSON output uses the
.B .ndjson
extension.  The logger code defaults to CSV when the variable is absent; the packaged
environment file currently selects JSON.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_OUTPUT_DIR
Directory for hourly rotating output files.  The default is
.BR /var/log/maps-logger .
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_DISK_WARN_MB
Write a warning when free space on the output filesystem falls below this many megabytes.
The value must be a positive integer.  The default is 500.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_USERNAME
Broker user name.  Unset connects without credentials.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_PASSWORD_FILE
File containing the broker password.  Requires
.BR MAPS_LOGGER_USERNAME .
Trailing line breaks are ignored.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_KEYSTORE
PKCS12 or JKS keystore holding the client certificate for mutual TLS.  Requires an
.B ssl://
URL and
.BR MAPS_LOGGER_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE .
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE
File containing the keystore password.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_TRUSTSTORE
PKCS12 or JKS trust store holding the broker certificate or its CA.  Requires an
.B ssl://
URL and
.BR MAPS_LOGGER_TRUSTSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE .
Without it the JVM default trust store is used.  Host name verification is always enabled.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_TRUSTSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE
File containing the trust store password.
.TP
.B MAPS_LOGGER_RETENTION_DAYS
Used by the compression timer: delete compressed files older than this many days.
0 or unset keeps files forever.
.PP
Secrets are only read from files, never from this file or the command line.  Keep them in
.I /etc/maps-logger/credentials/
owned
.B root:maps-logger
with mode 0640.  They are re-read on every reconnect..SH EXAMPLE
.EX
MAPS_LOGGER_URL=ssl://127.0.0.1:1895
MAPS_LOGGER_TOPIC=4817/#,/tak/cot/#
MAPS_LOGGER_QOS=1
MAPS_LOGGER_FORMAT=json
MAPS_LOGGER_OUTPUT_DIR=/var/log/maps-logger
MAPS_LOGGER_DISK_WARN_MB=500
MAPS_LOGGER_USERNAME=maps-logger
MAPS_LOGGER_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/maps-logger/credentials/mqtt-password
MAPS_LOGGER_KEYSTORE=/etc/maps-logger/credentials/logger-client.p12
MAPS_LOGGER_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/maps-logger/credentials/keystore-password
MAPS_LOGGER_TRUSTSTORE=/etc/maps-logger/credentials/broker-trust.p12
MAPS_LOGGER_TRUSTSTORE_PASSWORD_FILE=/etc/maps-logger/credentials/truststore-password
.EE
.SH APPLYING CHANGES
After editing the file, restart the service:
.PP
.EX
sudo systemctl restart maps-logger
.EE
.PP
Individual settings may instead be overridden with a systemd drop-in created by:
.PP
.EX
sudo systemctl edit maps-logger
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/maps-logger/env
Primary service environment file.  It is installed as a Debian conffile and is preserved
across normal package upgrades.
.TP
.I /etc/maps-logger/credentials/
Credential files referenced by the
.B *_FILE
variables; directory mode 0750, owned
.BR root:maps-logger .
.TP
.I /var/log/maps-logger/
Default output directory, owned by the
.B maps-logger
service account with mode 0750.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR maps-logger (8),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR maps-apps (7)
.SH AUTHOR
MapsMessaging B.V.
